a. Glob Pediatr Health. 2020;7:2333794X20968718. doi: 10.1177/2333794X20968718 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Bingham PM, Sukhudyan B, Hakobyan A. Pediatric neurology far from home: globalization, guidelines, and standards of care. Pediatr Neurol. 2015;52:1-4. doi: 10.1016/j.pediatrneurol.2014.10.002 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Moreno-Zambrano S, Sandrone S, Meza-Venegas J, et al. Exploring the key factors behind neurophobia: a systematic review of the English, Spanish and Portuguese literature. Brain Disord. 2021;2:11. [ Google Scholar ] 21. Laureta E, Moshé SL. State of training in child neurology 1997-2002. Neurology. 2004;62:864-869. doi: 10.1212/01.wnl.0000118646.34143.4a [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Gilbert DL, Horn PS, Kang PB, et al. Child neurology recruitment and training: views of residents and child neurologists from the 2015 AAP/CNS Workforce Survey. Pediatr Neurol. 2017;66:89-95. doi: 10.1016/j.pediatrneurol.2016.08.018 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Lamb DL. National Resident Matching Program, Results and Data: 2022 Main Residency Match®. National Resident Matching Program; 2022. [ Google Scholar ] 24. Murray RB, Larkins S, Russell H, et al. Medical schools as agents of change: socially accountable medical education. Med J Aust. 2012;196:653. doi: 10.5694/mja11.11473 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Reddy AT, Lazreg SA, Phillips RL, et al. Toward defining and measuring social accountability in graduate medical education: a stakeholder study. J Grad Med Educ. 2013;5:439-445. doi: 10.4300/JGME-D-12-00274.1 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Corley J. The rise of neurology in Haiti. Lancet Neurol. 2019;18:30-31. doi: 10.1016/S1474-4422(18)30431-9 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Becker-Barroso E. For neurologists in Cuba, hope is not embargoed. Lancet Neurol. 2009;8:1088-1089. doi: 10.1016/S1474-4422(09)70314-X [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google S